    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "47v7bo2",
      "content": "Gravitation is the force by which every object in the universe attracts every other object. This force is responsible for:"
    },
    {
      "id": "v3d5a0c",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Falling of objects on Earth</li><li>Motion of planets around the Sun</li><li>Motion of moon around Earth</li><li>Formation of tides</li></ul>",
        "Falling of objects on Earth",
        "Motion of planets around the Sun",
        "Motion of moon around Earth",
        "Formation of tides"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uvxn885",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "hc23ryj",
      "src": "/books/Precis/SSC COMPLETE GK/images/image_hc23ryj.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w98n1on",
      "content": "The force of gravitation is a universal force, which means it acts between all objects having mass."
    },
    {
      "id": "4jze48f",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "UNIVERSAL LAW OF GRAVITATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lhsojxy",
      "content": "The Universal Law of Gravitation was given by Sir Isaac Newton. According to this law:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jh5u5bn",
      "content": "Every object in the universe attracts every other object with a force which is:"
    },
    {
      "id": "fi392nh",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Directly proportional to the product of their masses</li><li>Inversely proportional to the square of the distance between their centres</li></ul>",
        "Directly proportional to the product of their masses",
        "Inversely proportional to the square of the distance between their centres"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pv6b1q6",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "y7nsv11",
      "src": "/books/Precis/SSC COMPLETE GK/images/image_y7nsv11.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "65kg8fu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Mathematical Formula"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1s97ky2",
      "content": "F = G × (m₁m₂ / r²) Where:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ev52ai7",
      "content": "F = gravitational force m₁ = mass of first object"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9q68a6t",
      "content": "m₂ = mass of second object"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "72tuijf",
      "content": "r = distance between the centres G = gravitational constant"
    },
    {
      "id": "l1c3lhn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Value of Gravitational Constant"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y4q7bzu",
      "content": "G = 6.67 × 10⁻¹¹ N m² / kg²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v8wwv3d",
      "content": "This value is constant everywhere in the universe."
    },
    {
      "id": "hgjp87z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EFFECTS OF GRAVITATIONAL FORCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tbefecn",
      "content": "Gravitational force is responsible for:"
    },
    {
      "id": "1wan8sl",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Objects falling towards Earth</li><li>Planets revolving around the Sun</li><li>Formation of tides</li><li>Weight of bodies</li><li>Holding atmosphere to Earth</li></ul>",
        "Objects falling towards Earth",
        "Planets revolving around the Sun",
        "Formation of tides",
        "Weight of bodies",
        "Holding atmosphere to Earth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ef3bkzn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "FREE FALL"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j5338fr",
      "content": "When an object falls towards the Earth under the influence of gravitational force only, it is said to be in free fall."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rsjhyc8",
      "content": "In free fall:"
    },
    {
      "id": "vcuzlpe",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Only gravitational force acts</li><li>Air resistance is neglected</li></ul>",
        "Only gravitational force acts",
        "Air resistance is neglected"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uz1ng6w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Acceleration Due to Gravity (g)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5u7xx3b",
      "content": "The acceleration produced in a body due to gravitational pull of Earth is called acceleration due to gravity."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "js8mzv6",
      "content": "Symbol: g"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qkouuay",
      "content": "Value on Earth = 9.8 m/s² It is constant for all objects."
    },
    {
      "id": "p3qubzc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MASS AND WEIGHT"
    },
    {
